  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Opt `asset` in/out of the set a KEEPER may name as `rebalance_swap`'s\\n`asset_out`. Auth: admin.\\n\\nWhy this exists: `rebalance_swap` takes a caller-supplied path and\\n`amount_out_min` with no on-chain price oracle, and the same keeper can\\ncall `rebalance_withdraw` first in the SAME transaction \\xe2\\x80\\x94 so without a\\nbound the reachable amount is an entire invested position, not the idle\\nfloat. Every hop of the path is checked against this list, not just the\\noutput (an endpoint-only check is trivially routed around via\\n`[allowed, EVIL, allowed]`).\\n\\n**What this does NOT do.** It narrows the total-loss case; it does not\\neliminate it. Allowlisting ASSETS says nothing about pool DEPTH: a\\ncompromised keeper can seed the canonical pair between two allowlisted\\nassets with dust and still dump a whole position into it at\\n`amount_out_min = 1`. The real residual bound is the depth of the\\nshallowest canonical pair among allowlisted assets \\xe2\\x80\\x94 which an attacker can\\ninfluence. Only the T3 oracle floor closes this; do not read this l",
      "name": "set_swap_asset",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "asset",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "allowed",
          "type_": "bool"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": []
    }
  },
